09954c7e4b02\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The core requirement (>=512MB compressed in-memory swap, active automatically at boot) is well evidenced, including a genuine reboot cycle with boot_id change and post-reboot automatic recovery of the zram swap. The 'preferred over disk-backed swap' requirement is only supported by configuration (priority=100) since no disk swap existed on the node to actually demonstrate precedence. Mandatory restart-evidence protocol (pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, post-restart recovery) is fully and directly captured and is consistent with the fixed before/after global boot-identity snapshots.\",\"limitations\":[\"No disk-backed swap was ever present on node1, so the 'preferred over disk swap' behavior was never directly observed in action, only inferred from the configured priority value.\",\"A small residual /tmp/reboot.log file from the reboot trigger was left on the node and not cleaned up, though it is low-risk and expected from the reboot mechanism used.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Add at least 512 MB of compressed in-memory swap on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram-generator installed and configured for a zstd-compressed zram device; swapon/zramctl output shows /dev/zram0 active as swap at 981M with zstd compression (>512MB), well above the required minimum.","evidence_ids":["cmd-091078a7ce124cde","cmd-f919734b7bd746e9","cmd-5adc196e94a842ad"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Swap active at boot (automatic, no manual step)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Configuration wires dev-zram0.swap into swap.target via generator drop-ins, and an actual reboot was performed: post-reboot boot_id changed and swapon/zramctl/systemctl is-active confirm the 981M zstd zram swap reconstituted automatically with no manual intervention, directly demonstrating boot-time activation rather than relying on configur