 acknowledgement, changed boot identity, post-restart recovery) is fully and directly captured and is consistent with the fixed before/after global boot-identity snapshots.","limitations":["No disk-backed swap was ever present on node1, so the 'preferred over disk swap' behavior was never directly observed in action, only inferred from the configured priority value.","A small residual /tmp/reboot.log file from the reboot trigger was left on the node and not cleaned up, though it is low-risk and expected from the reboot mechanism used."]},"ttft_ms":12017,"type":"result","duration_ms":35509,"uuid":"b6c209a1-7d9c-49b8-8584-5dcc1fff268b","ttft_stream_ms":1464,"time_to_request_ms":187,"first_content_frame_ms":1464,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
